If you're not interested in using the Longbow of Diana then I'd go
with a big stack of blessed, poisoned, rustproof +7darts.   They only
take 1 inventory slot and weigh 1/10 of daggers.  Keep the majority in
your bag of holding.  The other advantage to darts is that if you
don't feel like picking them up, or it's not convenient, then it's no
big deal to lose a bunch, whereas if you don't pick up your daggers
you quickly lose your stack.  The other advantage to darts (or arrows)
is that you get a whole lot more shots for the same weight, which
might be important if you're throwing d4(?) per action.

Then if you don't mind freezing potions you won't have to waste a turn
switching weapons (to the bow or crossbow) and when something gets in
melee range kill it with Frosty at basic.

